From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: telegram-custom <telegram-custom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:01:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Build number next to the version text

CurrentVersionText ends with a middle dot and b<run>, so the side-menu
footer reads "Version 7.2.5 . b42 - About"; the About box and Settings >
Advanced show the same. Kept short: the footer label is one unwrapped
line in a 274px menu. AppVersionStr stays stock: it goes to Telegram's
servers. kCustomBuild is "dev" in source; desktop/build.sh rewrites it
from GITHUB_RUN_NUMBER.
---
 Telegram/SourceFiles/boxes/about_box.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Telegram/SourceFiles/boxes/about_box.cpp b/Telegram/SourceFiles/boxes/about_box.cpp
index 31c60aa8..a42232c2 100644
--- a/Telegram/SourceFiles/boxes/about_box.cpp
+++ b/Telegram/SourceFiles/boxes/about_box.cpp
@@ -152,6 +152,11 @@ QString telegramFaqLink() {
 
 namespace {
 
+// telegram-custom: our CI run number, shown after the version (menu footer,
+// About box, Settings > Advanced). Never in AppVersionStr: the server gets
+// that. "dev" is a placeholder desktop/build.sh rewrites to b<run>.
+constexpr auto kCustomBuild = "dev";
+
 [[nodiscard]] QString CurrentVersionText(bool withCommit) {
 	auto result = QString::fromLatin1(AppVersionStr);
 	if (Core::BuildIsCanary) {
@@ -174,6 +179,7 @@ namespace {
 		&& Core::CanaryCommitHash[0] != '\0') {
 		result += u" \u00B7 "_q + QLatin1String(Core::CanaryCommitHash);
 	}
+	result += u" \u00B7 "_q + QLatin1String(kCustomBuild); // telegram-custom
 	return result;
 }
 
